Curated(
    varp: "tutorial",
    tracks: "Tutorial Island progress. 0 is a fresh account; 130 ends the survival curriculum; ^tutorial_complete = 1000 ends the whole island.",
    states: {
        1:   "open the player controls",
        4:   "click the door to leave the room",
        10:  "follow the path, talk to the survival expert",
        20:  "open your inventory",
        30:  "cut down the tree",
        40:  "use the tinderbox on the logs",
        50:  "open your skills",
        60:  "talk to the survival expert",
        70:  "catch shrimp at the fishing spot",
        80:  "use the shrimp on the fire",
        90:  "catch and cook another shrimp",
        120: "go through the gate and follow the path",
        130: "opened the gate to the chef",
    },
    note: Some("0 is the default value of a fresh account and appears in no states entry because no script assigns it -- the RuneScape Guide conversation has not happened yet; tutorial.rs2:49 only compares against it, never writes it. No script ever assigns %tutorial = 2 (confirmed by ontology_xref.rs::tutorial_states): the October-2006 comment block at runescape_guide.rs2:27-31 only comments out a case 2 : read of %tutorial (line 5) and an assignment of a DIFFERENT varp, %tutorial_progress = 2 (line 29) -- not an assignment of %tutorial itself. 3 IS a live bare-literal write (tutorial.rs2:145), but practically unreachable: it fires only inside a branch gated by %tutorial = 2, which nothing ever sets. Do not add 0, 2, or 3 as milestones."),
)
